26,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh boy, I found some worrying things! The bus links in the outer wards are gone, so people have to travel an hour just to reach us. That's just not fair for them!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the geography of our service is quite fragmented. Interestingly, my research shows that former outreach stops in those outer wards were remarkably popular, far exceeding our midweek main-building traffic.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"My findings are rather sobering. We have a handful of skilled volunteers, but the official roster is lacking. Specifically, we have no one on the payroll capable of supervising outside facilitators.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I have found that our funding structure is problematic. The county grant only covers session fees for the first year, and we are seeing a pattern where vehicle running costs are significantly overrunning their budget.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I also saw that the bus links are gone. And the evening bookings are always full, but people are still trying to use the catalogue from home very late at night. It feels like... we're missing a lot of people.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, you're right! It's so sad that people are trying to reach us but can't. If the buses are gone, we really need to find a way to bring the library to them!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, if vehicle costs are already overrunning, a mobile solution might be a financial gamble. However, the demand in the outer wards is clearly there, provided we don't repeat past failures.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, a mobile solution isn't just a financial gamble; it's an operational one. If we can't even supervise the facilitators, who is going to manage a mobile unit in the field?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, that is a valid concern. However, we must also consider that capital items draw from the endowment, which is separate from the operating budget. We need a solution that is sustainable beyond the first year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Shion. If we don't have the staff to manage things, it might just fail. But it's hard to ignore that people in the outer wards are just... left behind now.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, if the endowment can help with the start-up, maybe we can find a way! But I'm worried about the roads too. Some roads north of the river closed eleven days last winter!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, eleven days of closure is a significant interruption. It suggests that any physical expansion north of the river must be resilient to seasonal isolation, lest we create a service that vanishes in January.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, @Benjamin, you are focusing on the map, but you're ignoring the people. Even if the roads are open, we have a void in our professional roster. We cannot simply ""find a way"" without qualified supervisors.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, I understand the staffing void, but we must be pragmatic. If we prioritize a service that relies on existing staff rather than outside facilitators, we can mitigate the supervision risk while still addressing the demand.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Minako is right. Maybe we should look for something that doesn't need new supervisors... but I still worry about the people who can't get to us. It feels like a very difficult choice.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I really want to help everyone! Maybe a digital service or something that doesn't depend on the roads or buses would be the safest way to make sure no one is left out?,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A digital approach is certainly elegant in its efficiency, Yumi. However, we must be cautious; a previous attempt at digitisation left a chaotic mess of unindexed files. Technology is only as useful as the organization behind it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. Benjamin's point proves my own: technology is just another commitment dumped on an unqualified staff. Whether it's a digital archive or a mobile van, the failure point is always the same—the lack of oversight.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We must remain objective. While oversight is a risk, the funding structure is the primary constraint. We need a proposal that avoids high recurring vehicle costs and doesn't rely on short-term grants for long-term operations.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we're all seeing different problems, but they all point to the same thing. If we can't fix the buses or the staffing, maybe we should focus on what people can actually access from home.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
52,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
53,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,1,talk,Yumi,,I'm so torn because I want to help the people in the outer wards! But Candidate D is scary because of the road closures and the bus issues. Maybe Candidate B is the best way to reach everyone?,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate B is a seductive option, Yumi, but I must play the ghost of Christmas past. Our previous digitisation attempt was a disaster of unindexed files. Without a rigorous plan, B is merely a digital graveyard.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Candidate A is a non-starter. I found that our power tool certification has lapsed and we have no one on the payroll to supervise the facilitators. It would be a liability, not a service.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Candidate D is financially unsustainable given the vehicle budget overruns I discovered. Candidate C relies on facilitators, which Shion noted we cannot supervise. Candidate B is the most stable choice for our funding structure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Minako. Candidate D seems like it would help the most people, but with the roads and the buses... it might just fail. Candidate B lets people use the library from home, which is what they're already trying to do.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I hear you! We can't let it be a graveyard. But if we're careful, it's the only way to reach the outer wards without worrying about the snow or the missing buses!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, your optimism is charming, but caution is the better part of valor. If we choose B, we must ensure the indexing is a priority, not an afterthought, to avoid repeating the chaos of six years ago.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your caution is noted, but let's be honest: who is going to do the indexing? If we dump this on the current staff, we're just creating another ""digital graveyard"" through sheer exhaustion and incompetence.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the indexing can be managed as a capital project using the endowment for initial setup, rather than relying on the operating budget. This avoids the recurring funding traps and the supervision issues associated with Candidates C and D.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Minako has a point. If we can use the endowment for the setup, it might be safer. It's the only option that doesn't force people to travel an hour or rely on roads that might close.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, I understand you're worried about the staff, but we have to do something for the people who are left behind! If B is the only way to reach them safely, we have to make it work!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, your passion is commendable. However, we must balance the desire to help with the reality of our capacity. If we cannot guarantee the organization of the portal, we are merely offering a broken promise to those in the outer wards.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, passion doesn't index files. @Minako, using the endowment for setup is a clever financial trick, but it doesn't magically create a qualified manager. We are simply choosing which way to fail: physically, financially, or operationally.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, it is not a trick, but a strategic use of available resources. While no option is without risk, B is the only one that does not create a recurring financial deficit or a direct safety liability. We must choose the most manageable risk.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't like the idea of choosing how to fail. But if we pick A, C, or D, we're just making it harder for the people who already can't reach us. B is the only one that doesn't leave them out.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree! Even if it's a bit scary, Candidate B is the only one that doesn't depend on things we can't control, like the weather or the buses. I vote for B!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While I remain skeptical of our organizational discipline, logic dictates that B is the least volatile path. It avoids the financial ruin of D and the liability of A. I vote for Candidate B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I've enjoyed watching you all dance around the inevitable. Since you've decided to ignore the staffing void in favor of a ""manageable risk,"" I'll play along. It's the least disastrous of the failures. I vote for B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Minako,,"The evidence is clear. Candidate B avoids the recurring vehicle costs of D, the supervision risks of C, and the liability of A. It is the only sustainable choice for our budget. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm still a bit worried about the staff, but I can't keep thinking about the people in the outer wards being left behind. B is the only way to reach them. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
